{"title":"Non-Euclidean","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"container\">\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#The_Hardy–Weinberg_Configuration_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Hardy–Weinberg Configuration Theorem</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Corollary\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Corollary</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h1><span id=\"The_Hardy.E2.80.93Weinberg_Configuration_Theorem\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Hardy–Weinberg_Configuration_Theorem\">The Hardy–Weinberg Configuration Theorem</span></h1>\n<p>\nLet <em>S</em> be a segment of unit length representing the total allele space,\npartitioned into two subsegments of lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> satisfying\n</p>\n<div class=\"math\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f18257ababbe7bd31c7532c7110fe4a31aa1653.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p+q=1.\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>\nConstruct the square on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<div class=\"theorem\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem\">Theorem</span></h2>\n<p>\nThe partition of the unit square induced by the decomposition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />\ndetermines three regions having areas\n</p>\n<div class=\"math\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e5c713703a0df8f7eb9df793c170ec71e058fad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^2,\\qquad 2pq,\\qquad q^2,\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf774bed12159cf7cff200a2f3f4f7e57d3d2f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^2+2pq+q^2=1.\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>\nFurthermore, if successive constructions are performed by selecting\neach side independently according to the same partition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />,\nthen the induced area partition remains invariant under iteration.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"proof\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span></h2>\n<p>Since</p>\n<div class=\"math\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86af10af9fd6b4e3994ab5ba26168d10ca1fddd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p+q)^2=p^2+2pq+q^2,\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/8/cb88a84e20b604fb12926beec0999146fc88151a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p+q=1,\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9a3a49f4c8dfd86433da4883ca415afc8241d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1=(p+q)^2=p^2+2pq+q^2.\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>\nThe square therefore decomposes into two squares of areas\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bb97ca2ab6cdd3823e982b86f796662e4a58c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" />, together with two congruent rectangles of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79ccffd0d1686be982eed9fdcb75f35551e8cb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />.\nCombining the congruent rectangles yields a region of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd2b31e6ccda58585b85f5b6c50bf0286973c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" />.\nIndependent selection of the horizontal and vertical subdivisions\npreserves this decomposition under every iteration.\n</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:right;\">&#9633;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"corollary\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Corollary\">Corollary</span></h2>\n<div class=\"math\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/923f6cc3fc53989712d42e550d326b22453b5b69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^2:2pq:q^2\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>forms an invariant area ratio.\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101416\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 58/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2705/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31839:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018101416 and revision id 287597. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}